  ('49845388-581b-5168-9d77-3ab937447cc2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A classmate suggests adding dialogue to sentence 12, such as Lucia saying "We did it." What is the best reason to keep sentence 12 as it is?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Narratives written in the first person are not allowed to include dialogue from other characters.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-rule"},{"text":"Sentence 12 is the narrative's conclusion, and conclusions should never include actions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-function"},{"text":"Lucia has not been introduced yet, so the reader would not know who was speaking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character-introduction"},{"text":"The silent gesture suits a quiet booth during a live ceremony and lets the reader infer their shared relief.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The silent gesture suits a quiet booth during a live ceremony and lets the reader infer their shared relief.$q$, $q$A squeeze on the shoulder shows the relief without stating it, and it fits a setting where talking would be out of place. Lucia is introduced in sentence 6, so the reader already knows who Lucia is.$q$, 'draft', '8f0f64dc-fe36-5d75-abac-cdcc4eb28841')
