   $q$The city had no choice but to delay the stadium renovation because steel prices rose. Which verb most precisely completes the sentence "The rising cost of steel ______ the city to delay the stadium renovation."?$q$, $q$[{"text":"allowed","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"},{"text":"helped","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-verb"},{"text":"forced","is_correct":true},{"text":"encouraged","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$forced$q$, $q$"Forced" shows that the city had no choice, which matches the situation in the stem. "Encouraged" suggests a gentle push toward a choice the city could have refused.$q$, 'draft', null)
