   $q$Read the sentence: "The reason why the bakery closed early is because the oven broke." Which revision is the most concise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reason the bakery closed early is because the oven broke.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundancy-remains"},{"text":"The reason why the bakery closed early was that the oven broke down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase-remains"},{"text":"The bakery closed early, so the oven broke.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The bakery closed early because the oven broke.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bakery closed early because the oven broke.$q$, $q$"The reason why ... is because" says the idea of cause three times; one "because" is enough. The "so" choice is concise but reverses cause and effect.$q$, 'draft', null)
