  ('9b3bd9ba-f3fe-5eb4-aa35-901e26a8dc0d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-precise-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$After three seasons of sifting through layers of ash and silt, an archaeology team uncovered a carved bone flute. The writer wants a sentence that builds suspense by saving the discovery for the very end. Which choice does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A carved bone flute, after three seasons of sifting through ash and silt, was what the team uncovered.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"awkward-inversion"},{"text":"The team uncovered a carved bone flute after three seasons of sifting through layers of ash and silt.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"loose-not-periodic"},{"text":"After three seasons of sifting through layers of ash and silt, the team finally uncovered a carved bone flute.","is_correct":true},{"text":"After three seasons of sifting through layers of ash and silt, the team uncovered many ancient objects.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After three seasons of sifting through layers of ash and silt, the team finally uncovered a carved bone flute.$q$, $q$Placing the long introductory phrase first and the flute last creates a periodic sentence that delays the key detail. The choice that begins "The team uncovered a carved bone flute" contains the same facts but announces the flute immediately, so there is no suspense.$q$, 'draft', null)
