   $q$New soil samples weaken, but do not disprove, the theory that a canal was dug entirely by hand. Which verb most precisely completes the sentence "The new soil samples ______ the long-held theory that the canal was dug entirely by hand."?$q$, $q$[{"text":"undermine","is_correct":true},{"text":"mention","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"understates-claim"},{"text":"confirm","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"refute","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$undermine$q$, $q$"Undermine" means weaken without fully overturning, which matches the stem. "Refute" means prove false, which overstates what the samples show.$q$, 'draft', null)
