   $q$Which choice is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The ferns unfurl in early spring, by midsummer; their fronds shade the entire creek bank.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-semicolon"},{"text":"The ferns unfurl in early spring by midsummer, their fronds shade the entire creek bank.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"The ferns unfurl in early spring, by midsummer their fronds shade the entire creek bank.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"},{"text":"The ferns unfurl in early spring; by midsummer, their fronds shade the entire creek bank.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The ferns unfurl in early spring; by midsummer, their fronds shade the entire creek bank.$q$, $q$The boundary between the two independent clauses falls after "spring," and a semicolon correctly marks it. Placing the semicolon after "midsummer" leaves "by midsummer" stranded and creates a comma splice after "spring."$q$, 'draft', null)
