   $q$Read the sentence: "The printing press made books far cheaper to produce ___ literacy spread more quickly across Europe in the following century." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"produce, as a result,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"produce; as a result,","is_correct":true},{"text":"produce as a result,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"produce, as a result;","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-semicolon"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$produce; as a result,$q$, $q$"As a result" is a transitional phrase, not a conjunction, so the independent clauses must be separated by a semicolon placed before it. With only commas around it, the sentence is a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
