   $q$The writer wants to add a thesis after sentence 4 that captures the analysis both paragraphs develop. Which sentence works best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad's evidence shows that the Kessel River Bridge is in poor condition and will soon need to be replaced.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Haddad's evidence shows that the false alarms make the sensors more trouble than they are worth on most bridges.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-key-evidence"},{"text":"Haddad's evidence shows that the sensors can reveal hidden damage but raise too many false alarms to act on alone.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad's evidence shows that sensors are more accurate than human inspectors and should take over bridge safety.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-source"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad's evidence shows that the sensors can reveal hidden damage but raise too many false alarms to act on alone.$q$, $q$Paragraph 1 shows the sensors finding hidden damage and paragraph 2 shows the false alarms that require human judgment, so a thesis naming both fits. The "more trouble than they are worth" choice ignores the cracked bearing the sensors helped find.$q$, 'draft', '90aee6ac-600b-53b0-917e-2e2927ad6d83')
