   $q$A parallelogram has a base of $10$ cm and a height of $6$ cm. A straight cut along a height line splits it into a right triangle with a base of $3$ cm and a trapezoid. What is the area of the trapezoid in square centimeters?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$60$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-whole-parallelogram-area"},{"text":"$9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-the-triangle-area"},{"text":"$51$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$42$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-halve-triangle-area"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$51$$q$, $q$The whole parallelogram has area $10 \times 6 = 60$, and the triangle has area $\frac{1}{2} \times 3 \times 6 = 9$, so the trapezoid has area $60 - 9 = 51$ square centimeters. As a check, its bases are $7$ and $10$: $\frac{1}{2} \times 17 \times 6 = 51$. The choice $42$ subtracts $18$, the triangle without the half.$q$, 'draft', null)
